# UI Anti-Slop

One vocabulary for the three UI skills: `ui-direction` (concept before code), `ui-craft`
(implementation), `review-ui-ux` (review). The creator and the reviewer judge by the same list.

## Why slop happens

- **Distributional convergence.** With no direction a model emits the most probable design:
  Inter, indigo-on-white, centered hero, three cards, fade-up on scroll. Every "safe" default
  is a vote for the average. (Anthropic, *Improving frontend design through skills*)
- **A ban list alone fails.** Ban purple and the output moves to the *next* most probable look
  ("second-wave slop": cream + serif + terracotta; near-black + one neon accent; broadsheet).
  The cure is a **positive direction derived from the subject**, with this list as a guard rail.
- **Slop is a stack, not a tell.** One default (Inter for body text) is fine. Five defaults
  together are slop. Score density, not presence.
- **Behavioral slop** is the half nobody screenshots: missing states, no validation, no focus
  ring. Models learn from code snapshots, not from using flows.

## Core principles

1. **Direction comes from the subject.** Industry, materials, vernacular, printed artefacts,
   the client's own numbers and names. Not from "modern, clean, minimal".
2. **Spend boldness in one place.** Exactly one signature element; everything else quiet.
   Before finishing, remove one element.
3. **Distinctive look, conventional behavior** (Jakob's Law). Navigation placement, link
   affordance, form patterns, and keyboard behavior stay standard.
4. **Structure must encode information.** Borders, numbering, eyebrows, dividers, badges exist
   only when they carry meaning.
5. **Never invent proof.** No made-up stats, logos, testimonials, customers, or "Live" chips.
6. **If the brief names a look, follow it** — even if that look is on the list below.
7. **Don't claim checks that weren't run.** No browser → say so.

## Tell catalog

Tiers: **T1** — recognizable as AI within ~3 seconds by a layperson (must fix).
**T2** — obvious to anyone who builds UI (should fix). **T3** — weak alone, damning in a stack.

### Color
| Tier | Tell | Fix |
|---|---|---|
| T1 | Purple→blue / violet→indigo gradient on hero or background; radial "hero blobs" | 4–6 named colors with roles, derived from the subject |
| T1 | Gradient text (`bg-clip-text`) on headlines | Solid ink; emphasis by size/weight |
| T2 | Untouched framework palette (`indigo-500` primary, `emerald-500` success) | Own tokens; tune hue/chroma to the palette |
| T2 | Second-wave palettes used by reflex: cream `#F4F1EA` + terracotta `~#D97757`; near-black + acid green/vermilion | Justify from the subject or choose again |
| T2 | Brand color on more than 3 surfaces | Accent on the primary action + at most one other element |
| T3 | Gradient borders, decorative gradient washes, glows | Tone steps between surfaces |
| T3 | Gray text on colored backgrounds | Tint/shade of the background hue |
| T3 | Dark mode = inverted light mode | Re-tune each token for dark |

### Typography
| Tier | Tell | Fix |
|---|---|---|
| T1 | Inter / Roboto / Arial / Open Sans / Lato / system-ui as the *only* face | Choose a face for the subject; state the choice before coding |
| T2 | Re-converged substitutes used by default: Space Grotesk, Plus Jakarta Sans, Geist | Vary across projects; pick by mood, not habit |
| T2 | Accent on one headline word ("Build *faster*" — italic/colored/serif swap) | Let the sentence carry itself |
| T2 | Tracked ALL-CAPS eyebrow above every heading; mono for decorative meta labels | Only where it encodes information |
| T2 | Meta strings "A · B · C"; labels "WORD — fragment" | Plain sentence-case labels |
| T3 | Framework size ramp verbatim (12/14/16/18/24/30/36/48/60/72) | Modular ratio (1.2 / 1.25 / 1.333), ≤5 sizes |
| T3 | Close weights (400 vs 600); body at 600 | Extreme contrast (200–300 vs 700–900); body 400 |
| T3 | Headlines ≥48px with default tracking | −0.02 to −0.05em, leading 0.85–1.05 |

### Layout & composition
| Tier | Tell | Fix |
|---|---|---|
| T1 | Stock page order: pill badge → centered headline → 2 CTAs → logo row → 3 feature cards → pricing → CTA band | Sections as claims with proof; neighbors use different structures |
| T1 | Three equal icon cards with the icon in a tinted rounded square | Structure follows content (list, table, diagram, one large proof) |
| T2 | Fully centered page, no alignment axis | Left-aligned grid; ≤3 shared left edges |
| T2 | Every section the same height/padding/heading size | Rhythm: section gaps clearly larger than internal gaps, varied |
| T2 | 01/02/03 markers on content that is not a sequence | Number only real steps |
| T3 | Big number + small label + stat row as hero | Open with the subject's most characteristic element |
| T3 | Glass pill floating nav; fake grey-bar dashboard as hero art | Real product, real data |

### Components & surfaces
| Tier | Tell | Fix |
|---|---|---|
| T1 | SaaS card kit: one radius (16–24px) + same soft shadow everywhere; cards in cards | Radius by role (child ≤ parent); shadows only on floating layers |
| T2 | Card with shadow + border + tinted fill at once | Pick one separation method |
| T2 | Glassmorphism / backdrop-blur without depth meaning | Opaque surfaces with tone steps |
| T2 | Default icon set at default size, the usual five (zap, shield-check, bot, sparkles, rocket) | Fewer icons; icons only where they speed recognition |
| T3 | "→" appended to every link/CTA; same hover-lift on every card | Affordance via convention; hover only where clickable |
| T3 | Colored thick left border on a rounded card as decoration | Border only for state |

### Motion
| Tier | Tell | Fix |
|---|---|---|
| T2 | Same fade-and-slide-up on every section on scroll; count-up stats | One orchestrated moment; user-triggered motion explains change |
| T3 | Drifting blobs, pulsing cards, shimmer that answers no question | Delete |
| T3 | Bounce/elastic easing, `transition: all`, linear UI easing | ease-out in, ease-in out; transform/opacity only |

### Copy & content
| Tier | Tell | Fix |
|---|---|---|
| T1 | Invented round stats (10x, 99.9%, 10,000+), fake logos/testimonials | Delete anything unsourced; list sample content for replacement |
| T1 | Placeholder people/brands (Jane Doe, Sarah Johnson, Acme, Globex), lorem ipsum | Real or clearly marked sample content |
| T2 | Filler verbs: unlock, supercharge, empower, elevate, seamless, streamline | Say what the product does, in the user's words |
| T2 | Emoji in headings and bullets | Remove |
| T3 | Generic CTAs ("Get started", "Submit", "Learn more") | Outcome label ("Save changes", "Book a table") |
| T3 | Empty state = generic illustration + two lines that fit any product | Specific reason + direct action |

### Behavioral slop
| Tier | Tell | Fix |
|---|---|---|
| T1 | `outline: none` without `:focus-visible` replacement | Visible focus ring, ≥3:1 against adjacent colors |
| T1 | Missing loading / empty / error / disabled states | Design all of them |
| T2 | Forms with no validation, placeholder-as-label, pre-disabled submit | Visible labels, inline errors, focus first error |
| T2 | Critical actions only visible on hover; color-only status | Always reachable; text/icon + color |
| T2 | No `prefers-reduced-motion` variant | Keep content, drop travel |

## Craft thresholds (checkable)

**Type.** 1–2 families. Body 16–20px (≥16px on mobile inputs), line-height 1.45–1.6, measure
45–75ch (hero 30–45ch). Display ≥3× body on marketing pages; ≤3 visible sizes on dense app
screens. Real punctuation (curly quotes, “…”, en/em dashes). `tabular-nums` for compared numbers.

**Color.** Contrast text ≥4.5:1, large text (≥24px or ≥18.66px bold) and UI boundaries/icons
≥3:1 (WCAG 1.4.3 / 1.4.11). Color never the sole carrier of meaning (1.4.1). ≤3 contrast
treatments per view.

**Space & shape.** One spacing scale (4/8/12/16/24/32/48/64/96/128). Groups separated more than
items within them. Radius: one scale by role, nested radius concentric.

**Targets.** ≥24×24 CSS px (WCAG 2.5.8); ≥44px on touch (Apple 44pt, Material 48dp).

**Motion.** 100–400ms; ~100ms for toggles, 200–300ms for dialogs, nothing ≥500ms; entrances
slightly longer than exits; stagger 60–90ms; travel 16–32px.

**Feedback timing.** 0.1s feels instant; >1s needs an indicator; 2–10s spinner; ≥10s percent-done
+ cancel. Loaders appear after ~150–300ms and stay ≥300ms. Skeletons match final dimensions.

**Accessibility floor.** WCAG 2.2 AA, including 2.4.11 Focus Not Obscured (sticky headers →
`scroll-padding`), 2.5.7 drag alternative, 1.4.10 reflow at 320px, never disable zoom.

## Slop score

Count tells by tier on the reviewed surface: `T1×3 + T2×2 + T3×1`.
- 0–3 — distinctive or deliberately neutral
- 4–8 — template-leaning; fix T1/T2 first
- ≥9 — reads as AI-generated; redo direction, don't patch

A tell is exempt when `DESIGN.md` or the brief explicitly chooses it — record the exemption.

